    [33m        Inputs are converted to float type.[39;49;00m
    [33m    metric : str or callable, optional[39;49;00m
    [33m        The distance metric to use. If a string, the distance function can be[39;49;00m
    [33m        'braycurtis', 'canberra', 'chebyshev', 'cityblock', 'correlation',[39;49;00m
    [33m        'cosine', 'dice', 'euclidean', 'hamming', 'jaccard', 'jensenshannon',[39;49;00m
    [33m        'kulczynski1', 'mahalanobis', 'matching', 'minkowski',[39;49;00m
    [33m        'rogerstanimoto', 'russellrao', 'seuclidean', 'sokalmichener',[39;49;00m
    [33m        'sokalsneath', 'sqeuclidean', 'yule'.[39;49;00m
    [33m    **kwargs : dict, optional[39;49;00m
    [33m        Extra arguments to `metric`: refer to each metric documentation for a[39;49;00m
    [33m        list of all possible arguments.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Some possible arguments:[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        p : scalar[39;49;00m
    [33m        The p-norm to apply for Minkowski, weighted and unweighted.[39;49;00m
    [33m        Default: 2.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        w : array_like[39;49;00m
    [33m        The weight vector for metrics that support weights (e.g., Minkowski).[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        V : array_like[39;49;00m
    [33m        The variance vector for standardized Euclidean.[39;49;00m
    [33m        Default: var(vstack([XA, XB]), axis=0, ddof=1)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        VI : array_like[39;49;00m
    [33m        The inverse of the covariance matrix for Mahalanobis.[39;49;00m
    [33m        Default: inv(cov(vstack([XA, XB].T))).T[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        out : ndarray[39;49;00m
    [33m        The output array[39;49;00m
    [33m        If not None, the distance matrix Y is stored in this array.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    Returns[39;49;00m
    [33m    -------[39;49;00m
    [33m    Y : ndarray[39;49;00m
    [33m        A :math:`m_A` by :math:`m_B` distance matrix is returned.[39;49;00m
    [33m        For each :math:`i` and :math:`j`, the metric[39;49;00m
    [33m        ``dist(u=XA[i], v=XB[j])`` is computed and stored in the[39;49;00m
    [33m        :math:`ij` th entry.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    Raises[39;49;00m
    [33m    ------[39;49;00m
    [33m    ValueError[39;49;00m
    [33m        An exception is thrown if `XA` and `XB` do not have[39;49;00m
    [33m        the same number of columns.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    Notes[39;49;00m
    [33m    -----[39;49;00m
    [33m    The following are common calling conventions:[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    1. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'euclidean')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the distance between :math:`m` points using[39;49;00m
    [33m       Euclidean distance (2-norm) as the distance metric between the[39;49;00m
    [33m       points. The points are arranged as :math:`m`[39;49;00m
    [33m       :math:`n`-dimensional row vectors in the matrix X.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    2. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'minkowski', p=2.)``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the distances using the Minkowski distance[39;49;00m
    [33m       :math:`\\|u-v\\|_p` (:math:`p`-norm) where :math:`p > 0` (note[39;49;00m
    [33m       that this is only a quasi-metric if :math:`0 < p < 1`).[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    3. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'cityblock')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the city block or Manhattan distance between the[39;49;00m
    [33m       points.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    4. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'seuclidean', V=None)``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the standardized Euclidean distance. The standardized[39;49;00m
    [33m       Euclidean distance between two n-vectors ``u`` and ``v`` is[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          \\sqrt{\\sum {(u_i-v_i)^2 / V[x_i]}}.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       V is the variance vector; V[i] is the variance computed over all[39;49;00m
    [33m       the i'th components of the points. If not passed, it is[39;49;00m
    [33m       automatically computed.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    5. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'sqeuclidean')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the squared Euclidean distance :math:`\\|u-v\\|_2^2` between[39;49;00m
    [33m       the vectors.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    6. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'cosine')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the cosine distance between vectors u and v,[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          1 - \\frac{u \\cdot v}[39;49;00m
    [33m                   {{\\|u\\|}_2 {\\|v\\|}_2}[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       where :math:`\\|*\\|_2` is the 2-norm of its argument ``*``, and[39;49;00m
    [33m       :math:`u \\cdot v` is the dot product of :math:`u` and :math:`v`.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    7. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'correlation')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the correlation distance between vectors u and v. This is[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          1 - \\frac{(u - \\bar{u}) \\cdot (v - \\bar{v})}[39;49;00m
    [33m                   {{\\|(u - \\bar{u})\\|}_2 {\\|(v - \\bar{v})\\|}_2}[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       where :math:`\\bar{v}` is the mean of the elements of vector v,[39;49;00m
    [33m       and :math:`x \\cdot y` is the dot product of :math:`x` and :math:`y`.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    8. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'hamming')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the normalized Hamming distance, or the proportion of[39;49;00m
    [33m       those vector elements between two n-vectors ``u`` and ``v``[39;49;00m
    [33m       which disagree. To save memory, the matrix ``X`` can be of type[39;49;00m
    [33m       boolean.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    9. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'jaccard')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m       Computes the Jaccard distance between the points. Given two[39;49;00m
    [33m       vectors, ``u`` and ``v``, the Jaccard distance is the[39;49;00m
    [33m       proportion of those elements ``u[i]`` and ``v[i]`` that[39;49;00m
    [33m       disagree where at least one of them is non-zero.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    10. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'jensenshannon')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Jensen-Shannon distance between two probability arrays.[39;49;00m
    [33m        Given two probability vectors, :math:`p` and :math:`q`, the[39;49;00m
    [33m        Jensen-Shannon distance is[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m           \\sqrt{\\frac{D(p \\parallel m) + D(q \\parallel m)}{2}}[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        where :math:`m` is the pointwise mean of :math:`p` and :math:`q`[39;49;00m
    [33m        and :math:`D` is the Kullback-Leibler divergence.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    11. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'chebyshev')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Chebyshev distance between the points. The[39;49;00m
    [33m        Chebyshev distance between two n-vectors ``u`` and ``v`` is the[39;49;00m
    [33m        maximum norm-1 distance between their respective elements. More[39;49;00m
    [33m        precisely, the distance is given by[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m           d(u,v) = \\max_i {|u_i-v_i|}.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    12. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'canberra')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Canberra distance between the points. The[39;49;00m
    [33m        Canberra distance between two points ``u`` and ``v`` is[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          d(u,v) = \\sum_i \\frac{|u_i-v_i|}[39;49;00m
    [33m                               {|u_i|+|v_i|}.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    13. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'braycurtis')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Bray-Curtis distance between the points. The[39;49;00m
    [33m        Bray-Curtis distance between two points ``u`` and ``v`` is[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        .. math::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m             d(u,v) = \\frac{\\sum_i (|u_i-v_i|)}[39;49;00m
    [33m                           {\\sum_i (|u_i+v_i|)}[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    14. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'mahalanobis', VI=None)``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Mahalanobis distance between the points. The[39;49;00m
    [33m        Mahalanobis distance between two points ``u`` and ``v`` is[39;49;00m
    [33m        :math:`\\sqrt{(u-v)(1/V)(u-v)^T}` where :math:`(1/V)` (the ``VI``[39;49;00m
    [33m        variable) is the inverse covariance. If ``VI`` is not None,[39;49;00m
    [33m        ``VI`` will be used as the inverse covariance matrix.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    15. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'yule')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Yule distance between the boolean[39;49;00m
    [33m        vectors. (see `yule` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    16. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'matching')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Synonym for 'hamming'.[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    17. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'dice')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Dice distance between the boolean vectors. (see[39;49;00m
    [33m        `dice` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    18. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'kulczynski1')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the kulczynski distance between the boolean[39;49;00m
    [33m        vectors. (see `kulczynski1` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    19. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'rogerstanimoto')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Rogers-Tanimoto distance between the boolean[39;49;00m
    [33m        vectors. (see `rogerstanimoto` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    20. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'russellrao')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Russell-Rao distance between the boolean[39;49;00m
    [33m        vectors. (see `russellrao` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    21. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'sokalmichener')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Sokal-Michener distance between the boolean[39;49;00m
    [33m        vectors. (see `sokalmichener` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    22. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'sokalsneath')``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the Sokal-Sneath distance between the vectors. (see[39;49;00m
    [33m        `sokalsneath` function documentation)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    23. ``Y = cdist(XA, XB, f)``[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Computes the distance between all pairs of vectors in X[39;49;00m
    [33m        using the user supplied 2-arity function f. For example,[39;49;00m
    [33m        Euclidean distance between the vectors could be computed[39;49;00m
    [33m        as follows::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          dm = cdist(XA, XB, lambda u, v: np.sqrt(((u-v)**2).sum()))[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        Note that you should avoid passing a reference to one of[39;49;00m
    [33m        the distance functions defined in this library. For example,::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          dm = cdist(XA, XB, sokalsneath)[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m        would calculate the pair-wise distances between the vectors in[39;49;00m
    [33m        X using the Python function `sokalsneath`. This would result in[39;49;00m
    [33m        sokalsneath being called :math:`{n \\choose 2}` times, which[39;49;00m
    [33m        is inefficient. Instead, the optimized C version is more[39;49;00m
    [33m        efficient, and we call it using the following syntax::[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m          dm = cdist(XA, XB, 'sokalsneath')[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    Examples[39;49;00m
    [33m    --------[39;49;00m
    [33m    Find the Euclidean distances between four 2-D coordinates:[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> from scipy.spatial import distance[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> import numpy as np[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> coords = [(35.0456, -85.2672),[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...           (35.1174, -89.9711),[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...           (35.9728, -83.9422),[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...           (36.1667, -86.7833)][39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> distance.cdist(coords, coords, 'euclidean')[39;49;00m
    [33m    array([[ 0.    ,  4.7044,  1.6172,  1.8856],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 4.7044,  0.    ,  6.0893,  3.3561],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.6172,  6.0893,  0.    ,  2.8477],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.8856,  3.3561,  2.8477,  0.    ]])[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    Find the Manhattan distance from a 3-D point to the corners of the unit[39;49;00m
    [33m    cube:[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> a = np.array([[0, 0, 0],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [0, 0, 1],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [0, 1, 0],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [0, 1, 1],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [1, 0, 0],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [1, 0, 1],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [1, 1, 0],[39;49;00m
    [33m    ...               [1, 1, 1]])[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> b = np.array([[ 0.1,  0.2,  0.4]])[39;49;00m
    [33m    >>> distance.cdist(a, b, 'cityblock')[39;49;00m
    [33m    array([[ 0.7],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 0.9],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.3],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.5],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.5],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 1.7],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 2.1],[39;49;00m
    [33m           [ 2.3]])[39;49;00m
    [33m[39;49;00m
    [33m    """[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
        [90m# You can also call this as:[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
        [90m#     Y = cdist(XA, XB, 'test_abc')[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
        [90m# where 'abc' is the metric being tested.  This computes the distance[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
        [90m# between all pairs of vectors in XA and XB using the distance metric 'abc'[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
        [90m# but with a more succinct, verifiable, but less efficient implementation.[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
    [90m[39;49;00m
        XA = np.asarray(XA)[90m[39;49;00m
        XB = np.asarray(XB)[90m[39;49;00m
    [90m[39;49;00m
        s = XA.shape[90m[39;49;00m
        sB = XB.shape[90m[39;49;00m
    [90m[39;49;00m
        [94mif[39;49;00m [96mlen[39;49;00m(s) != [94m2[39;49;00m:[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mraise[39;49;00m [96mValueError[39;49;00m([33m'[39;49;00m[33mXA must be a 2-dimensional array.[39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
        [94mif[39;49;00m [96mlen[39;49;00m(sB) != [94m2[39;49;00m:[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mraise[39;49;00m [96mValueError[39;49;00m([33m'[39;49;00m[33mXB must be a 2-dimensional array.[39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
        [94mif[39;49;00m s[[94m1[39;49;00m] != sB[[94m1[39;49;00m]:[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mraise[39;49;00m [96mValueError[39;49;00m([33m'[39;49;00m[33mXA and XB must have the same number of columns [39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m[90m[39;49;00m
                             [33m'[39;49;00m[33m(i.e. feature dimension.)[39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
    [90m[39;49;00m
        mA = s[[94m0[39;49;00m][90m[39;49;00m
        mB = sB[[94m0[39;49;00m][90m[39;49;00m
        n = s[[94m1[39;49;00m][90m[39;49;00m
    [90m[39;49;00m
        [94mif[39;49;00m [96mcallable[39;49;00m(metric):[90m[39;49;00m
            mstr = [96mgetattr[39;49;00m(metric, [33m'[39;49;00m[33m__name__[39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m, [33m'[39;49;00m[33mUnknown[39;49;00m[33m'[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
            metric_info = _METRIC_ALIAS.get(mstr, [94mNone[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mif[39;49;00m metric_info [95mis[39;49;00m [95mnot[39;49;00m [94mNone[39;49;00m:[90m[39;49;00m
                XA, XB, typ, kwargs = _validate_cdist_input([90m[39;49;00m
                    XA, XB, mA, mB, n, metric_info, **kwargs)[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mreturn[39;49;00m _cdist_callable(XA, XB, metric=metric, out=out, **kwargs)[90m[39;49;00m
        [94melif[39;49;00m [96misinstance[39;49;00m(metric, [96mstr[39;49;00m):[90m[39;49;00m
            mstr = metric.lower()[90m[39;49;00m
            metric_info = _METRIC_ALIAS.get(mstr, [94mNone[39;49;00m)[90m[39;49;00m
            [94mif[39;49;00m metric_info [95mis[39;49;00m [95mnot[39;49;00m [94mNone[39;49;00m:[90m[39;49;00m
                cdist_fn = metric_info.cdist_func[90m[39;49;00m
                _extra_windows_error_checks(XA, out, (mA, mB), **kwargs)[90m[39;49;00m
                [94mreturn[39;49;00m cdist_fn(XA, XB, out=out, **kwargs)[90m[39;49;00m
            [94melif[39;49;00m mstr.startswith([33m"[39;49;00m[33mtest_[39;49;00m[33m"[39;49;00m):[90m[39;49;00m
